---
import Product from '../../layouts/Product.astro';
import CaseworkFlow from '../../components/CaseworkFlow.astro';
import { products } from '../../data/products';
const product = products.find((p) => p.key === 'casework')!;
---
<Product
  product={product}
  heading="Review requests and record decisions."
  description="Government teams need to assign review requests, see who is responsible and when a decision is due, then record the outcome. Registry Casework manages that work and returns the decision to the service that requested the review."
>
  <section id="product-example" class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="casework-example-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">One example: a licence correction</p>
        <h2 id="casework-example-title">Assign the request, track its due date, and record the decision.</h2>
        <p>A licence holder reports that the professional register lists the wrong permitted activities. The licensing application receives the correction request and sends it for staff review in Registry Casework. If a certificate is missing, the licensing application collects it and submits a new review request. Each review has its own due date and history of staff actions.</p>
      </div>
      <CaseworkFlow />
      <p class="product-note">An approval records the staff decision. Permission to change a register remains controlled by that register’s rules.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="casework-inbox-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Practical capabilities</p>
        <h2 id="casework-inbox-title">See who is responsible, what is due, and what staff decided.</h2>
        <p>Review requests can arrive from a register, a case system, or another service. Registry Casework places each request in the agreed queue and records its progress until staff reach a decision.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="product-facts">
        <article><h3>Assign work and take responsibility</h3><p>Send each kind of request to the right queue. An officer takes responsibility for a request and can release it if they cannot continue. Supervisors can reassign work when staffing changes.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Track the time allowed</h3><p>Set the time allowed for each review step and the working-day calendar. Staff can see when a request is due. Registry Casework identifies when follow-up is due, and a connected service sends any email or SMS notices.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Record and return the decision</h3><p>Record an approval, refusal, request for changes, or other configured outcome. The service that requested the review receives the result and takes the next step under its own rules.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="fit" class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="casework-fit-title">
    <div class="section-inner product-fit">
      <div class="section-heading compact">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it fits your organization</p>
        <h2 id="casework-fit-title">Add staff review to a service you already run.</h2>
        <p>Registry Casework manages staff reviews. An implementation connects it to the screens, sign-in and existing service your staff use. It can accept review requests on its own or connect to proposed changes in Base Registry Engine. Connecting another register requires additional integration work.</p>
      </div>
      <dl>
        <dt>Your institution defines the review</dt><dd>Decide which requests need staff review, which team receives each kind, which outcomes are allowed, and when the decision is due.</dd>
        <dt>Choose who delivers the implementation</dt><dd>Aubex, another delivery partner, or your own team can provide or adapt staff screens, connect sign-in and the service that requests reviews, and test the complete process. Agree who will host, operate and support the service.</dd>
        <dt>Keep control of record changes</dt><dd>Registry Casework returns the staff decision. The service that requested the review uses it under the rules for that service. Registry Casework does not change the register itself.</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="developers" class="section" aria-labelledby="casework-developers-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading compact">
        <p class="eyebrow">For developers and implementers</p>
        <h2 id="casework-developers-title">Prepare a proposed change for review.</h2>
        <p>The introductory tutorial prepares and validates matching Base Registry Engine and Registry Casework configuration. It does not execute a review or apply a change. Continue with the <a href="https://docs.registrystack.org/configure/casework/">configuration guide</a> and <a href="https://docs.registrystack.org/operate/casework/">operations documentation</a> for implementation.</p>
        <p><a class="inline-cta" href={product.tutorialHref}>{product.tutorialLabel} →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Product>
